      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Disabling smooth motion across the entire menu would be great, too.\nSome users get uncomfortable from menu animations, even in Desktop PC games.\nI don't mind the animations, but if it helps users are comfortable I'm all for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-12T20:39:39.549Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The smoothing for the raycast from the player hand is absolutely a welcome effect. However, having both ends of the raycast have that delay leads more to the feeling of the raycast being unresponsive rather than smooth. Instead, having the hand end of the ray be locked to the hand visually while the tip is what moves smoothly would tremendously help with the feeling, leading to a feeling of weight to the cursor rather than of it being unresponsive.",
